render-ports' table with a running router (host.pid.self), for port's apply
(rowt #s73). The stand-in router is a `sleep`, which a SIGHUP ends where sing-box
would reload in place. So on both sides the in-place reload does not take, the
full restart cannot start (the fake engine exits at once), the change is undone
and the router does not come back either: the whole fallback chain, compared
end to end. Slow by nature (two readiness waits), hence the cases' PARITY_TIMEOUT.

  port rm guest            guest leaves the table and stays gone — undoing a
                           removal writes the table WITHOUT the name, which is
                           what rm already wrote
  port add 7892 guest --final escape
                           the same row again: nothing to write, but the apply
                           runs, its port never opens, and the undo drops the
                           row (a row that is not served must not stay)
  port list                running, so every row says "not answering"
